window.MONSTER_CHUNK_129 = [{"name":"Giant Hornet","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"vermin","init":1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":15,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +5 natural, -1 size","hp":45,"hd":"7d8+14","hdvalue":7,"fort":7,"ref":3,"will":3,"immunities":["vermin traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"bite +9 (1d3+5), sting +9 (1d4+5 plus poison)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"poison"}],"strength":20,"dexterity":12,"constitution":15,"wisdom":13,"charisma":11,"baseatk":5,"cmb":11,"cmd":22,"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":9},{"skill":"Survival","value":1,"special":"+4 orient direction"}],"sq":[{"type":"pheromone"}],"environments":["any temperate land","any warm land"],"organizations":["solitary","cluster (2-5)","nest (11-20)"],"treasure":"standard or otherwise","description_visual":"This massive horse-sized hornet has a black body with white markings on the thorax and abdomen and a cruel looking rapier-length stinger.","group":"Hornet","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Sting-injury; save DC 21; frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d3 Dexterity damage; cure 2 consecutive saves. The save DC is Constitution-based and includes a +2 racial bonus."},{"type":"Pheromone","kind":"Ex","details":"The first time a giant hornet is successfully hit in combat, it releases a fear pheromone that heightens the aggressiveness of all giant hornets within 50 ft. All affected giant hornets receive a +1 morale bonus on attack rolls for the remainder of the encounter and fight without penalty even while disabled or dying."}],"description":"Giant hornets are larger, more aggressive versions of normal hornets.\n\nThey are generally inoffensive if left alone, but if provoked, become very deadly opponents. Giant hornets have a society structure consisting of two distinct classes: workers and the queen.\n\nWorkers spend their time pulling nectar from flowers and carrying it to the nest where they feed the young, the queen, and the other hornets. They are also the hornets involved in defending the nest and queen from attack.\n\nWhen aggressors are detected within 100 ft. of the nest, the workers fly out and patrol the area. Creatures that move within 20 ft. are attacked.\n\nThe queen's sole purpose is to lay eggs that ultimately hatch and grow into new hornets. She has no stinger and doesn't attack-workers kill most aggressors long before they reach the queen. Giant hornet builds its nest high above the ground in much the same way a standard wasp does.\n\nA giant hornet's nest has a curved flare at the top.\n\nGiant hornets attack by biting their foes, only relying on its stinger when threatened. During combat, it releases a pheromone that agitates all other giant hornets in the area, making them more aggressive.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Giant Moray Eel","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"animal","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +8 natural, -1 size","hp":52,"hd":"7d8+21","hdvalue":7,"fort":8,"ref":9,"will":3,"immunities":["disease","fear"],"weaknesses":["water dependency"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":5},{"type":"swim","speed":30}],"melee":"bite +11(2d6+9 plus disease and grab)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"gnaw"}],"strength":22,"dexterity":14,"constitution":16,"intelligence":1,"wisdom":12,"charisma":8,"baseatk":5,"cmb":12,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":24,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Stealth)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":10},{"skill":"Perception","value":7},{"skill":"Stealth","value":11},{"skill":"Swim","value":18}],"environments":["warm aquatic"],"organizations":["solitary","school (4-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature looks like an 8-foot long eel with yellowish-brown splotches on its back.","group":"Eel","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Disease","kind":"Ex","details":"Flesh Rot: Bite-injury; save Fort DC 13; onset 1 minute; frequency 1/day; effect 1d6 Con and 1d6 Cha damage; cure 2 consecutive saves. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Gnaw","kind":"Ex","details":"If a giant moray begins a round with a grabbed foe, it inflicts automatic bite damage (2d6+9 points of damage). A giant moray eel possesses a second set of jaws in its throat that aid in swallowing-it can make a second bite attack (+11 attack, 1d6+4) against a foe it has already grabbed."},{"type":"Water Dependency","kind":"Ex","details":"Giant moray eels can survive out of the water for 1 minute per point of Constitution (after that, see the Drowning rules)."}],"description":"The moray eel is a ferocious predator, capable of holding prey in its primary jaws while a smaller set of jaws inside its throat chews away bite-sized portions. Moray Eel Animal Companion Starting Statistics: Size Medium; AC +5 natural armor; Speed swim 30 ft.; Attack bite (1d8); Ability Scores Str 14, Dex 16, Con 12, Int 1, Wis 12, Cha 8; Special Qualities low-light vision, grab. 7th-Level Advancement: Size Large; AC +3 natural armor; Attack bite (2d6); Ability Scores Str +8, Dex -2, Con +4; Special Qualities gnaw.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Giant Moray Eel originally appeared in the First Edition Monster Manual (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1977) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Gilded Sea Serpent","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"dragon","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":4,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":30,"ac_touch":14,"ac_flat_footed":26,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +16 natural","hp":52,"hd":"5d12+20","hdvalue":5,"fort":9,"ref":8,"will":7,"dr":"5/gold","immunities":["paralysis and sleep","dragon traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":10},{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"bite +9 (1d8+1 plus poison)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"constrict","details":"1d8+1"},{"type":"poison"}],"strength":12,"dexterity":19,"constitution":16,"intelligence":7,"wisdom":16,"charisma":17,"baseatk":5,"cmb":6,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":20,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Swim-By Attack","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":11},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12},{"skill":"Survival","value":11},{"skill":"Swim","value":17}],"languages":["Draconic"],"environments":["temperate aquatic","warm aquatic"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","cluster (3-8)"],"treasure":"none (see below)","description_visual":"This serpent is about 8 ft. long and 2 ft. thick. Its body scales are small and smooth, with the brilliant luster of gold. It has a long, narrow crocodilian snout and a cluster of antenna-like whiskers sweeping back from just above its jaws.","group":"Sea Serpent","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":": Bite-injury; save Fort DC 15; frequency 1/round for 4 rounds; effect 1d4 Wis; cure 2 consecutive saves. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"One of the rarest of sea serpents, the gilded serpent is known for its glittering golden hide, and is often hunted for this skin, and for the powerful narcotic that can be made from its venom. In the wild, gilded sea serpents live on the most secluded islands and hidden lagoons, where they nest in sandy lairs and shallow, sun-warmed waters. Wealthy coastal lords have been known to acquire gilded sea serpent eggs or infants and raised them captivity. These serpents are usually revered as holy or prized as status symbols; captive gilded serpents that are mistreated quickly lose the will to live and die. The golden hide of a gilded serpent can be harvested and made into a single set of scale mail that fits a Medium or smaller creature. This armor is considered masterwork, and has the same properties as mithral scale armor. The poison of the gilded serpent can be milked or harvested as well, then made into a powerful narcotic drug called golden bliss. Gilded sea serpents flee danger when they can, using their ability to swim swiftly to evade danger as quickly as possible. If cornered or surprised, however, they lash out with their bite, and use their constriction attack if their prey is small enough. The venom of a gilded sea serpent numbs the flesh to pain and induces a state of catatonic stupor. Golden Bliss This drug is made from the venom of a gilded sea serpent. A serpent that is milked of its venom produces enough poison to make 2d4 doses of golden bliss per day. This requires a DC 15 Craft (alchemy or poison) check. When inhaled, the drug produces a euphoric catatonia and provides complete protection against mind-influencing magic and psionic incursion. GOLDEN BLISS Type: inhaled; Addiction severe, Fortitude DC 15 Price 40 gp Effects 1d3x10 minutes; +4 Charisma, immunity to mind-affecting effects and psionic incursion. Damage 4 Wisdom damage.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Gloom Haunt","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"undead","subtypes":["incorporeal"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"ac":18,"ac_touch":18,"ac_flat_footed":15,"ac_mods":"+5 deflection, +3 Dex","hp":57,"hd":"6d8+30","hdvalue":6,"fort":7,"ref":5,"will":7,"defensive_abilities":["incorporeal","channel resistance +2","shadowy resolve"],"immunities":["undead traits"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":50,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"incorporeal touch +7 (3d6+5 plus pain touch)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"shadow mastery"}],"dexterity":17,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":14,"charisma":20,"baseatk":4,"cmb":7,"cmd":25,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":16},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":14},{"skill":"Knowledge (any one)","value":8},{"skill":"Perception","value":13},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":13},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12,"special":"+16 in dim light, +8 in bright light"}],"sq":[{"type":"creeping shadows"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","gang (gloom haunt plus 2-4 shadows)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"A vaguely humanoid shape composed of darkness rises from the shadows.","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Creeping Shadows","kind":"Su","details":"Once per day, a gloom haunt can emanate an inky darkness in a 30-foot-radius burst as a standard action. This functions as a deeper darkness spell (CL 6th)."},{"type":"Incorporeal Touch","kind":"Su","details":"By passing part of its incorporeal body through a foe's body as a standard action, the gloom haunt inflicts 7d6 damage. This damage isn't negative energy-it manifests in the form of physical wounds and aches from supernatural aging. Creatures immune to magical aging are immune to this damage, but otherwise the damage bypasses all forms of damage reduction. A Fortitude save halves the damage inflicted."},{"type":"Pain Touch","kind":"Su","details":"A gloom haunt adds its Charisma modifier on damage rolls with its incorporeal touch. Additionally, the touch of a gloom haunt sends a wave of intense pain through the opponent's body. A creature touched must succeed on a DC 18 Fortitude save or be stunned for 1 round and shaken for 1d4+2 rounds thereafter. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Shadow Mastery","kind":"Su","details":"A gloom haunt is a creature of darkness. In areas of total darkness (including that created by its creeping shadows ability), a gloom haunt gains a +2 racial bonus on attack rolls, saves, and checks. These bonuses are not included in the statistics block."},{"type":"Shadowy Resolve","kind":"Su","details":"In areas of shadowy illumination or total darkness, a gloom haunts channel resistance increases to +4."}],"description":"Gloom haunts are believed to somehow be related to shadows though most learned scholars agree that people simply relate them to shadows because of their resemblance to said creatures. In actuality, gloom haunts are different creatures, unrelated to the aforementioned undead at all. While both prefer areas of gloom and darkness, and both seem to be formed of shadowstuff, that's where the similarities end.\n\nGloom haunts are vile evil creatures, who seem to have no ties to the living (i.e., scholars cannot find any reasonable explanation as to why they exist), though a few learned sages believe gloom haunts to be the spiritual remains of paladins who were sacrificed by evil clerics to their vile and dark gods. Gloom haunts are found haunting graves, dungeons, and catacombs. These creatures detest light (though they are not harmed by it) and move about at night when their natural coloration and abilities help them the most.\n\nA gloom haunt appears as a humanoid-shaped somewhat translucent creature formed of darkness. Two small pinpoints of red light function as eyes. A gloom haunt doesn't speak or utter any sounds.\n\nGloom haunts use their ability to hide in shadows to wait for living creatures to come close. When such a creature does, glooms haunt leap to the attack.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Gorilla Bear","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"magical beast","init":2,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":16,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +5 natural, -1 size","hp":42,"hd":"4d10+16 (+4)","hdvalue":4,"fort":8,"ref":6,"will":2,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"2 claws +8 (1d8+5 plus grab), bite +8 (1d8+5)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"constrict","details":"1d8+5"}],"strength":20,"dexterity":15,"constitution":18,"intelligence":2,"wisdom":12,"charisma":7,"baseatk":4,"cmb":10,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":22,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":11},{"skill":"Perception","value":9},{"skill":"Swim","value":11}],"environments":["warm forests"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","pack (3-6)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature resembles a massive gorilla with shaggy dark fur and the forepaws of a powerful bear. Its head appears to be a cross between a gorilla and bear.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","description":"Gorilla bears are the result of a magical crossbreeding and merging of two distinct species a gorilla and a black bear. A gorilla bear's fur is always dark and ranges in color from jet black to brownish-black. Its paws and ft. end in elongated nails, brown in color. A typical gorilla bear stands 8 ft. tall and weighs almost 1,700 pounds. Its eyes are always one of two colors crimson or emerald green. No other eye color has ever been seen on a gorilla bear (though legends speak of an immensely powerful white-Furred gorilla bear with eyes the color of amethysts).\n\nGorilla bears make their lairs in caves or caverns, often hidden among the twisted tangle of trees and shrubs of jungles. They are diurnal (daylight) hunters and feast on a diet of meat, savoring the taste of goblins and elves. A typical lair contains a mated pair and 1d4 young.\n\nGorilla bears are highly aggressive and attack their prey relentlessly.\n\nGorilla bears never retreat and always fight until either they are all dead or their opponents are all dead. Opponents that attempt to flee are usually run down. Gorilla bears attack with their claws, cutting huge chunks of flesh from a foe when a claw attack hits. When presented with the opportunity, gorilla bears grab their opponent and squeeze them until dead, gnashing and biting at a grappled foe with their pointed teeth. Slain prey is dragged back to the lair and divided among the young and adults.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Gorilla Bear originally appeared in the First Edition Fiend Folio (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1981) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Grey Spirit","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"NE","size":"Medium","type":"undead","subtypes":["incorporeal"],"init":3,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["frightful presence (30 ft., DC 17)"],"ac":17,"ac_touch":17,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+4 deflection, +3 Dex","hp":51,"hd":"6d8+24","hdvalue":6,"fort":6,"ref":5,"will":5,"defensive_abilities":["channel resistance +4","incorporeal","rejuvenation"],"immunities":["undead traits"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":30,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"incorporeal touch +8 (2d6 cold plus energy drain)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"energy drain","details":"1 level, DC 17"},{"type":"ravages of death gaze"}],"dexterity":16,"intelligence":11,"wisdom":11,"charisma":18,"baseatk":4,"cmb":7,"cmd":24,"feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (gaze)"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (incorporeal touch)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":11},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":13},{"skill":"Perception","value":12},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":9},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12}],"languages":["Common"],"sq":[{"type":"harbinger"}],"environments":["any land"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"The lone female figure is clad in long, flowing grey robes and scarves which whip around her wildly even in the absence of a strong wind. Her head is covered by a wrapped veil, shielding her face from those who would see it.","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Harbinger","kind":"Su","details":"The appearance of a grey spirit is usually a harbinger of some future catastrophe, such as a great storm or a shipwreck. Such events occur within 1d6 days of the sighting of a grey spirit. Note that the grey spirit doesn't cause this catastrophe, rather she predicts it."},{"type":"Ravages of Death Gaze","kind":"Su","details":"Any living creature that sees the face of a grey spirit suddenly knows her pain, frustration, and rage, and has glimpse of the anguish of what it is like to die broken hearted. Any opponent experiencing this tragic emotion must succeed on a DC 19 Will save or be stunned for 2d6 rounds. A creature stunned by a grey spirit is wrought with despair, weeping and wailing uncontrollably. A calm emotions spell ends this effect. This is a mind-affecting effect A creature who succeeds on the save cannot be affected by the same grey spirit's gaze for one day. The save DC is Charisma-based and includes a +2 bonus from the grey spirit's Ability Focus feat."},{"type":"Rejuvenation","kind":"Su","details":"In most cases, it's difficult to destroy a grey spirit through simple combat: the \"destroyed\" spirit restores itself in 2d4 days. Even the most powerful spells are usually only temporary solutions. The only way to permanently destroy a grey spirit is to confront her with irrefutable evidence of her loved one's death. The exact means varies with each spirit and may require a good deal of research, and should be created specifically for each different grey spirit by the GM."}],"description":"Many a sailor who ventures out into the trackless sea is destined never to look again on the loved ones he left behind. Either death or the lure of foreign lands keeps them from returning to those who wait patiently for them. A grey spirit, usually female, is the shade of someone who died heartbroken and alone, pining away on shore and ultimately dying of a broken heart while waiting for the return of a loved one from across the sea.\n\nA grey spirit attacks any creature that approaches her, her rage and frustration at having lost her loved one knowing no bounds. In melee, a grey spirit fails wildly with her ghostly arms and hands, screaming and cursing all the while. If an opponent proves to be particularly strong, a grey spirit pulls aside the cowl that covers her face.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Grimstalker","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"NE","size":"Medium","type":"fey","init":9,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":18,"ac_touch":15,"ac_flat_footed":13,"ac_mods":"+5 Dex, +3 natural","hp":52,"hd":"8d6+24","hdvalue":8,"fort":5,"ref":11,"will":7,"dr":"5/cold iron","speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"climb","speed":20}],"melee":"2 claws +9 (1d4+1 plus poison)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"sneak attack","details":"+3d6"}],"strength":12,"dexterity":21,"constitution":17,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":13,"charisma":16,"baseatk":4,"cmb":5,"cmd":20,"feats":[{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Stealthy"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":16,"special":"+20 jump"},{"skill":"Climb","value":20},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":18},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":11},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":13},{"skill":"Perception","value":12},{"skill":"Stealth","value":18,"special":"+26 in forests"},{"skill":"Survival","value":9}],"languages":["Aklo","Common","Elven"],"environments":["any forests"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (2-5)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature looks like a hairless elf, slender and graceful, with long arms that end in sharp claws. Its skin is brown and woody and resembles tree bark. It wears clothes made of leaves and vines.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Claw-injury; save Fort DC 17; frequency 1/ round for 6 rounds; effect 1d2 Dex; cure 2 saves. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"The grimstalker or banaan (as they prefer to call themselves) is a fey creature that doesn't share the beauty and goodness of its kin. Whereas other fey creatures have come to represent the beautiful or mischievous side of nature, the grimstalker most certainly reflects nature at its worst.\n\nThey are dark creatures, their hearts tainted with the foulest of evil.\n\nUnfortunate souls that wander into a forest guarded by grimstalkers are never seen again-except for their skulls, which the grimstalkers hang from the trees as a warning to those that would dare trespass into their domain.\n\nLong thought to be a form of intelligent plant because of their many plant-like features, grimstalkers skulk among the trees of the darkest forests. Even among sylvan communities of elves the grimstalkers are legendary as natural born assassins.\n\nGrimstalkers sometimes work with other evil fey such as redcaps (see their entry in this book); though such alliances are short and very rare, especially with the malevolent and untrustworthy redcap.\n\nIt is rumored that powerful evil druids often summon grimstalkers for nefarious purposes.\n\nGrimstalkers strike from ambush if possible, hiding among the trees and dropping on interlopers into their forest. A troupe of grimstalkers that set up an ambush make ample use of the terrain, as well as nets woven from living vines, snares, and pit traps. Grimstalkers also employ trained plant creatures such as assassin vines and scythe trees. In melee they are capable of fighting with their claws or with weapons-their favorite weapons being a sort of spiked quarterstaff and longbows knocked with poisoned arrows.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Gulper Eel","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"animal","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":2,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":15,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":13,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +4 natural, -1 size","hp":60,"hd":"8d8+24","hdvalue":8,"fort":8,"ref":8,"will":3,"speed":[{"type":"swim","speed":50}],"melee":"bite +9 (2d6+4 plus grab)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"swallow whole","details":"1d8+3 acid damage, AC 12, 6 hp"}],"strength":17,"dexterity":15,"constitution":14,"intelligence":1,"wisdom":12,"charisma":2,"baseatk":6,"cmb":10,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":22,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Swim-by Attack"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":11},{"skill":"Swim","value":15}],"environments":["any aquatic"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This strange being of the depths appears to be little more than a large mouth, flaccid body and dangling tail which glows with an unnatural red light.","group":"Eel","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","description":"This larger version of its more common cousin makes its home in deep tropical and temperate waters well below 3,000 ft. in depth. The gulper eel spends its life eating giant shrimp, and any other creatures which happen to arouse its senses.\n\nGulper eels spend most of their lives in the deepest and darkest parts of the oceans, rarely if ever venturing near the surface waters. Solitary creatures by nature, during mating season (colder months of the year), it is common to find a pair of these creatures dwelling together. During mating season, the female deposits her eggs (2-8) in the dirt and mass of plants on the ocean floor. Within two months the eggs hatch and the young swim free. Young are independent within 2 weeks after birth and venture out on their own shortly thereafter.\n\nA gulper eel averages 10 ft. in length but can grow to reach 30 ft. or more. Its body is long, sleek, and black in color and its tail ends in a luminous organ. Its eyes are small for its body and close to its snout. It massive mouth is lined with rows of sharpened teeth.\n\nGulper eels attempt to bite their prey, holding it before swallowing it whole. Because a gulper eel can unhinge its jaw and stretch its stomach, it can swallow opponents larger than itself.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Hellstoker Devil","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["devil","evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +8 natural","hp":37,"hd":"5d10+10","hdvalue":5,"fort":3,"ref":5,"will":6,"defensive_abilities":["fiery body","oily hide"],"dr":"5/good and silver","immunities":["fire","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10}],"sr":16,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"longspear +7 (1d8+3/x3) or 2 claws +7 (1d6+2)","ranged":"ranged touch +6 (bellows)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with longspear)","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":10,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":12,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"magic circle against good"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"maximized burning hands"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 5, 2d8 lemures 50% or 1 hellstoker 35%"}]}],"strength":15,"dexterity":13,"constitution":15,"intelligence":6,"wisdom":10,"charisma":10,"baseatk":5,"cmb":7,"cmd":18,"feats":[{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Maximize Spell-like Abilities (burning hands)"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":10},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":11},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":8},{"skill":"Perception","value":8},{"skill":"Survival","value":8}],"languages":["Infernal","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Hell)"],"organizations":["solitary","team (4-7)","retinue (8-13)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This man-sized creature has loosely hanging, rubbery flesh, grayish black in color, and its entire body is smeared with a yellowish-brown mucus. Its head is ovoid, devoid of hair, and sports upward curving horns. A hardened ridge of bone runs from its brow, across the top of its head, and disappears into its spine. Its long, serpentine tail is dark grayish-red.","group":"Devil","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Bellows","kind":"Ex","details":"A hellstoker can use its burning hands to light its bellows as a standard action. This allows the hellstoker to fire a jet of flame from its bellows in a line to a range of 30 ft., once per round as a standard action. It must make a successful ranged touch attack to hit a foe. A creature hit by the fire takes 1d8 points of fire damage and must succeed on a DC 15 Reflex save or catch on fire."},{"type":"Fiery Body","kind":"Ex","details":"The oil coating a hellstoker's body is highly flammable. As such, a hellstoker hit with a fire effect bursts into flames. This deals no damage to the hellstoker, and deals 1d6 points of fire damage to any creature touching or grappling the hellstoker. The fire burns for 10 rounds before extinguishing. This doesn't damage the hellstoker's oily hide; therefore, it still retains its racial bonus to Escape Artist checks (see oily hide below), and it can be caught on fire again."},{"type":"Oily Hide","kind":"Ex","details":"Hellstokers don't secrete oil naturally, but their constant contact with it leaves them coated with a thick layer of the substance at all times. This grants hellstokers a +10 racial bonus to Escape Artist checks (included in the statistics block). The oil cannot be washed off or removed. Additionally, if a hellstoker is hit with a fire effect, it bursts into flames. See the hellstoker's fiery body above for details."}],"description":"Hellstokers (or marnasoths) maintain the oil, made from the flesh of mortals, in the infernal boilers located on the lowest region of Hell. They are rarely encountered anywhere else, though on occasion a team or retinue of hellstokers enters the Material Plane in search of fuel. Most just wait for the foolhardy mortals that enjoy plane-hopping to pop into their realm where any number of devils finish them off, leaving their rotting carcasses to the hellstokers. When fuel is running low and the hellstokers are short on mortals, they form bands that hunt down and kill the least ranking devils (such as lemures), tossing their slain bodies into the boilers.\n\nHellstokers attack using their longspears or natural weapons. They sometimes use burning hands to set one another on fire, or they use it to ignite the oil in their bellows. When outnumbered, hellstokers usually use burning hands against their foes and then teleport away to safety.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","gear":"longspear, bellows"},{"name":"Homotherium","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"animal","init":2,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":15,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":13,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +3 natural","hp":51,"hd":"6d8+24","hdvalue":6,"fort":9,"ref":7,"will":3,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"bite +10 (1d6+6 plus grab plus bleed), 2 claws +10  (1d4+6 plus grab)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"bleed","details":"1"},{"type":"pounce"},{"type":"rake","details":"2 claws +10, 1d4+6"}],"strength":23,"dexterity":15,"constitution":19,"intelligence":2,"wisdom":12,"charisma":6,"baseatk":4,"cmb":10,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":22,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Run"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":10},{"skill":"Perception","value":9},{"skill":"Stealth","value":11,"special":"+15 in snowy areas"},{"skill":"Swim","value":10}],"environments":["cold forests","cold plains"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","den (6-10)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This white-furred cat has short forelegs in comparisons to its loping rear legs. Prominent fangs protrude from its upper jaw.","group":"Smilodon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","description":"This white-furred saber-toothed cat is a relative of the smilodon but makes its home in the arctic regions of the world. Its canines are much shorter than the smilodon (averaging only about 4-5 inches long) and its front legs are longer than its rear legs (similar to a hyena's leg structure).","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Huge Acid Quasi-elemental","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["acid","elemental","extraplanar"],"init":8,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["fumes (5 ft., Fort DC 18)"],"ac":20,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":16,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +8 natural, -2 size","hp":76,"hd":"8d10+32","hdvalue":8,"fort":6,"ref":10,"will":8,"dr":"5/-","immunities":["acid","elemental traits"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to water"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"swim","speed":80}],"melee":"2 slams +11 (1d8+5 plus 1d8 acid)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"acid"},{"type":"drench"}],"strength":21,"dexterity":18,"constitution":19,"intelligence":6,"wisdom":11,"charisma":11,"baseatk":8,"cmb":15,"cmd":29,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":9},{"skill":"Perception","value":11},{"skill":"Stealth","value":7},{"skill":"Swim","value":24}],"languages":["Aquan"],"environments":["any (Quasi-Plane of Acid)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"What was once a still puddle of green liquid rises up like a wave, lashing out with acid-dripping tendrils. In the midst of the pool, one can barely make out regions of darker green that form a vaguely human face.","group":"Quasi-elemental","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Acid","kind":"Ex","details":"Acid quasi-elementals are living creatures of acid; any melee hit deals acid damage. Creatures hitting an acid quasi-elemental unarmed or with natural attacks take acid damage as though hit by the quasi-elemental's slam attack."},{"type":"Acid Swimmer","kind":"Ex","details":"Acid quasi-elementals cannot swim in water. The swim speed given in the statistics block is their movement only through acid pools or the acidic nature of their environment on their home plane."},{"type":"Drench","kind":"Ex","details":"The quasi-elemental's touch puts out torches, campfires, exposed lanterns, and other open flames of nonmagical origin if these are of Large size or smaller. The creature can dispel magical fire as dispel magic (caster level equals the quasi-elemental's HD)."},{"type":"Fumes","kind":"Ex","details":"The fumes from an acid quasi-elemental's body act as an inhaled poison. Creatures within 5 ft. of an acid quasi-elemental must make succeed on a Fortitude save or take 1 point of Constitution damage each round. This poison doesn't have a frequency; a creature is safe as soon as it moves more than 5 ft. away from the acid quasi-elemental."},{"type":"Vulnerability to Water","kind":"Ex","details":"An acid elemental erupts in a violent chemical reaction when touched by water. An acid quasi-elemental takes 1d4 points of fire damage for each gallon of water poured into it. The reaction is so violent that all creatures within 5 ft. of the acid quasi-elemental when the water hits it must succeed on a DC 15 Reflex save or take the same damage. Pouring water onto an acid quasi-elemental requires a successful ranged touch attack. Water from other sources, such as spells or effects that create water but don't specify an amount in gallons, deal 1d4 points of fire damage per caster level to an acid quasi-elemental within its area of effect. Damage from water-based attacks, like the slam attack of a water elemental, is increased by 50% against an acid quasi-elemental. Note that this reaction doesn't occur when the acid quasi-elemental touches water, only when water touches the acid quasi-elemental."}],"description":"Nestled among the various elemental there lies a plane composed entirely of acid. It is a place of noxious fumes and roiling, bubbling, pools. Plane jumpers do well to avoid this place as it is considered by many to be one of the deadliest, if not the deadliest, of the elemental-based planes. Acid quasi-elementals rarely journey from their native plane, except when summoned. They don't like the Material Plane and when called to the place, are usually angered and always a bit uncomfortable. They have no trouble moving on land, but prefer the sanctity of their native plane to all others. At rest, an acid quasi-elemental is a clear puddle of liquid with a slightly green hue. It can rise up like a wave in a manner similar to a water elemental, or ooze along solid surfaces by sending out tendrils and pulling itself along. Wherever it travels, it leaves behind a shallow trough that emits wisps of smoke. Acid quasi-elementals are almost always encountered in large pools of acid when on the Material Plane and rarely leave these pools when combating foes. A favored tactic is to grab a foe and pull it into the quasi-elemental's acid pool, subjecting it to massive amounts of acid damage.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Huge Obsidian Quasi-elemental","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["earth","elemental","extraplanar"],"init":-1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":17,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +10 natural, -2 size","hp":76,"hd":"8d10+32","hdvalue":8,"fort":6,"ref":5,"will":6,"dr":"5/-","immunities":["elemental traits"],"resists":[{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20}],"melee":"2 claws +14 (2d6+8/19-20)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"death throes"},{"type":"molten glass","details":"2d8 fire, DC 18"}],"strength":26,"dexterity":8,"constitution":19,"intelligence":6,"wisdom":11,"charisma":11,"baseatk":8,"cmb":18,"cmd":27,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (claw)"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Attack","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":9},{"skill":"Perception","value":11},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":11},{"skill":"Stealth","value":2}],"languages":["Terran"],"environments":["any (Quasi-Plane of Obsidian)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature is a powerfully built, roughly humanoid-shaped monolith of black stone. Its hands end in wicked, serrated and jagged claws. No facial features can be discerned.","group":"Quasi-elemental","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Death Throes","kind":"Ex","details":"When reduced to 0 or less hit points, an obsidian quasi-elemental explodes in a cloud of razor-sharp bits of obsidian. A creature caught in the area can make a Reflex save for half damage. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Molten Glass","kind":"Ex","details":"A successful hit against an obsidian quasi-elemental with a piercing or slashing weapon (or piercing or slashing natural attack) that deals damage equal to its current HD opens a wound that spurts molten glass. The wound bleeds for 1d4 rounds and any creature within 5 ft. must make a Reflex save or take fire damage from the splash. A new save must be made each round the wound bleeds and a creature is within the area. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"In a quasi-realm where elemental water and elemental fire conjoin, there exists a pocket plane known as the Quasi-plane of Obsidian; a plane of barren wastes and blackened rock, of razor-sharp obelisks and fields of sharpened glass. Creatures native to this plane appear as blackened obsidian with jagged, serrated, or clear-cut angles and edges. Some have barbed spikes adorning their elemental forms. Obsidian quasi-elementals are usually encountered on their home plane or on the Plane of Fire. Still some can be found on the Obsidian Plain in the Plane of Molten Skies (see the City of Brass by Necromancer Games). Most, however, prefer the serenity that the Quasi-plane of Obsidian offers, and thus they rarely venture forth unless summoned. Obsidian quasi-elementals are deadly combatants and strike with their sharpened claws, ripping and tearing at their opponents. They are relentless in their attacks and never give quarter.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Ice Golem","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"construct","subtypes":["cold"],"init":-1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":16,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":16,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +8 natural, -1 size","hp":63,"hd":"6d10+30","hdvalue":6,"fort":2,"ref":1,"will":2,"dr":"5/adamantine","immunities":["cold","construct traits","magic"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to fire"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20}],"melee":"2 slams +9 (1d6+4 plus 1d6 cold)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"20-ft. cone, 3d6 cold damage, Reflex DC 15 for half, usable once every 1d4 rounds"},{"type":"cold","details":"1d6"}],"strength":18,"dexterity":9,"wisdom":11,"charisma":1,"baseatk":6,"cmb":11,"cmd":20,"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This automaton is nearly twice as tall as a normal human and seems to be chiseled from ice and snow.","group":"Golem","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"The save DC is Constitution-based and includes a +2 racial bonus."},{"type":"Cold","kind":"Ex","details":"An ice golem's body generates intense cold, dealing 1d6 points of damage with its touch. Creatures attacking an ice golem unarmed or with natural weapons take this same cold damage each time one of their attacks hit."},{"type":"Immunity to Magic","kind":"Ex","details":"An ice golem is immune to any spell or spell-like ability that allows spell resistance. In addition, certain spells and effects function differently against the creature, as noted below. Lightning-based effects slow an ice golem (as the spell) for 2d6 rounds. Cold-based effects heal all of its lost hit points."}],"description":"The ice golem is a humanoid formed of roughly chiseled ice, standing 10 ft. tall and weighing around 800 pounds. Ice golems at rest appear to be normal ice sculptures and are often mistaken as such (DC 20 Perception check to notice the creature is alive). An ice golem usually opens combat with its breath weapon. An ice golem never uses weapons or wears armor, preferring to attack with its powerful fists. Fire is an effective means of combating these creatures. Construction An ice golem's body must be constructed from a single block of ice weighing at least 1,000 pounds. The ice is treated with magical powders and unguents worth at least 500 gp. ICE GOLEM CL 12th; Price 19,600 gp Requirements Craft Construct, chill touch, cone of cold, geas/quest, polymorph any object, resist energy (cold), creator must be caster level 12th; Skill Craft (sculptures) DC 17; Cost 10,050 gp","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Ice Salamander","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["air","cold","extraplanar","water"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["bitter cold (10 ft.)"],"ac":18,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +7 natural","hp":59,"hd":"7d10+21","hdvalue":7,"fort":8,"ref":6,"will":4,"dr":"10/magic","immunities":["cold"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to fire"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"burrow","speed":20,"special":"ice and snow only"}],"melee":"spear +11 (1d8+4/x3 plus 1d6 cold) or 2 claws +10 (1d6+3 plus 1d6 cold)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","strength":16,"dexterity":12,"constitution":16,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":15,"charisma":12,"baseatk":7,"cmb":10,"cmd":21,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (spear)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":11},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":11},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":11},{"skill":"Perception","value":12},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":12},{"skill":"Stealth","value":11},{"skill":"Survival","value":12}],"languages":["Aquan","Common"],"sq":[{"type":"snow move"},{"type":"snow vision"}],"environments":["any (Plane of Water)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","gang (3-5)"],"treasure":"standard (spear)","description_visual":"This creature has the scaled upper torso of a humanoid, a snake-like head, and the lower body of a four-legged lizard with thick powerful legs. Its scales are icy blue and the creature's underbelly is white.","group":"Salamander","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Bitter Cold","kind":"Ex","details":"All creatures within 10 ft. of an ice salamander take 1d6 points of cold damage each round on the ice salamander's turn. Additionally, creatures that takes cold damage from the salamander's aura must succeed on a DC 16 Fortitude save or be staggered for 1 round. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Snow Move","kind":"Ex","details":"An ice salamander suffers no penalties for moving through snow-covered terrain."},{"type":"Snow Vision","kind":"Ex","details":"An ice salamander can see perfectly well in snowy conditions and doesn't take any penalties on Perception checks while in snow."}],"description":"Ice salamanders are malign creatures that dwell on the elemental planes where Water meets Air. Scholars speculate an entire plane (a para-elemental plane of cold or ice) exists where the Plane of Air and Plane of Water meet. There, the great ice salamanders make their homes carved into great icebergs or upon vast sheets of ice. Upon their home plane, the ice salamanders gather in large, loose tribes, led by the strongest member of the group. Infighting is common among tribal members and should a dispute escalate, it is usually settled in a makeshift arena where all participants fight to the death.\n\nWhen summoned to the Material Plane ice salamanders can be found in arctic regions where the temperatures are constantly freezing or lower (which to an ice salamander is still too warm). On the Material Plane, ice salamanders are often found acting as guards for high-level wizards or temple guardians for clerics of the frost gods. Some ice salamanders find their way to the Material Plane on their own, in areas where the elemental planes have spilled over to the Material Plane.\n\nAn ice salamander stands about 6 ft. tall with a serpentine head and the lower torso of a salamander. Its scales are blue mottled white, and its underbelly is stark white. Its eyes are ice blue and its pupils are dark. Cold seems to emanate from the creature at all times.\n\nIce salamanders jump headlong into melee, slashing their opponents with their wicked spears or claws. Prisoners are rarely taken, unless the ice salamanders are instructed to do so. Most of the time, prey is devoured as soon as it's killed.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Jolly Jelly","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"ooze","init":-5,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["gloom (30 ft., DC 14)"],"ac":10,"ac_touch":5,"ac_flat_footed":10,"ac_mods":"-5 Dex, +5 natural","hp":63,"hd":"6d8+36","hdvalue":6,"fort":8,"ref":-3,"will":-3,"immunities":["fire","ooze traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"3 slams +6 (1d6+2)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"pheromones"}],"strength":14,"dexterity":1,"constitution":22,"wisdom":1,"charisma":12,"baseatk":4,"cmb":6,"cmd":11,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","environments":["temperate land"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature appears to be a bright pink ooze speckled with spots of green, yellow, and blue. Scattered across the body of the ooze are small spiracles through which it apparently breathes.","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Aura of Gloom","kind":"Su","details":"Any living creature that comes within 30 ft. of a jolly jelly must succeed on a DC 14 Will save or take 1d2 points of Charisma damage. A new save must be made each round the creature remains in the area. A creature that takes 6 or more points of Charisma damage from this attack is automatically affected as if by a rage spell (CL 6th) with the exception that it cannot tell friend from foe. The affected creature remains enraged until it moves more than 30 ft. away from the jolly jelly. There is no save against the rage effect. This is a mind-affecting effect. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Pheromones","kind":"Ex","details":"Once per day, as a swift action, a jolly jelly can emit a cloud of pheromones containing the distilled essence of the positive emotions the jelly has consumed. This cloud covers a 20-foot-radius burst around the jelly. Living creatures in the cloud must succeed on a DC 19 Fortitude save or be affected as by a hideous laughter spell (CL 6th) for 2d4 rounds. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Jolly jellies are psychic vampires which feed on positive emotion. The mere presence of a jolly jelly causes living creatures in its vicinity to become dour and petulant. Often the victims of a jolly jelly descend into violence against one another as all traces of happiness and mirth are drained away by the creature. A jolly jelly needs no nourishment other than the emotions it drains from its victims. A jolly jelly can go several months between meals before the effects of starvation are noticed.\n\nJolly jellies are mostly active during sunrise and sunset, even underground. During daylight hours they are sedentary in their lair which if aboveground is usually under fallen trees or hollowed logs. Underground, jolly jellies dwell in damp caves and caverns.\n\nJolly jellies vary in size, but a typical specimen is 5 ft. across and weighs 100 pounds. A jolly jelly that has recently eaten (usually within the last 4 hours) is flushed with a deeper pink hue than one that hasn't.\n\nUnlike most oozes, a jolly jelly has no acid with which it can attack. Its only means of physical defense are slams from its multi-colored pseudopods. As a last-ditch defense, a jolly jelly can emit a cloud of pheromones containing the mirth it has absorbed from its victims. It is this laughter-inducing cloud that gave the jolly jelly its name.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Lamprey Swarm","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Tiny","type":"animal","subtypes":["aquatic","swarm"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":14,"ac_touch":14,"ac_flat_footed":12,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +2 size","hp":52,"hd":"8d8+16","hdvalue":8,"fort":8,"ref":10,"will":5,"defensive_abilities":["swarm traits"],"immunities":["weapon damage"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":5},{"type":"swim","speed":30}],"melee":"swarm (2d6 plus distraction and blood drain)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"0 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"distraction","details":"DC 16"}],"strength":5,"dexterity":15,"constitution":14,"intelligence":1,"wisdom":12,"charisma":2,"baseatk":6,"feats":[{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Swim)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":10},{"skill":"Perception","value":8},{"skill":"Swim","value":15}],"sq":[{"type":"amphibious"},{"type":"swarm traits"}],"environments":["temperate aquatic","warm aquatic"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","cluster (3-6 swarms)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"A black cloud of eel-like fish swims rapidly forward.","group":"Swarm","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Blood Drain","kind":"Ex","details":"Any living creature that takes damage from a lamprey swarm must succeed on a DC 16 Reflex save. On a failed save, several lampreys have attached themselves to the target and the creature takes 1d3 points of Constitution damage each round as the lampreys drain blood. This effect continues as long as the victim remains in the swarm and for 1d6 rounds after it leaves the swarm. The attached lampreys can be killed instantly by dealing at least 6 points of damage to the victim (any weapon or energy-based attacks work), ending the effect prematurely. A successful DC 16 Heal check reduces the duration by 1d6 rounds, ending the effect prematurely. The save DC and check DC are both Constitution-based."}],"description":"A lamprey swarm is a mass of lampreys numbering in the hundreds, possibly thousands. These creatures are attracted to living creatures in the water and quickly attach themselves to their targeted prey.\n\nLamprey swarms attack any living prey encountered in their paths, swimming over the creature and draining as much blood as possible. When their prey is dead, they move on, seeking out a new source of nourishment.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Large Gravity Elemental","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["elemental","extraplanar","gravity"],"init":10,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":18,"ac_touch":18,"ac_flat_footed":11,"ac_mods":"+2 deflection, +6 Dex, +1 dodge, -1 size, +0 natural","hp":76,"hd":"8d10+32","hdvalue":8,"fort":6,"ref":12,"will":6,"defensive_abilities":["distortion"],"dr":"5/-","immunities":["elemental traits","missile weapons","mass-dependent spells"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":100,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"2 slams +13 (1d6+3)","ranged":"missile +13) (damage by type)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"engulf"},{"type":"gravity field","details":"crush 4/day, 20 ft. radius, DC 17, 2d8 bludgeoning"}],"strength":16,"dexterity":23,"constitution":18,"intelligence":4,"wisdom":11,"charisma":11,"baseatk":8,"cmb":12,"cmd":31,"feats":[{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Throw Anything","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":12},{"skill":"Perception","value":11},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":11},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13}],"languages":["Gravity Manipulation"],"sq":[{"type":"perfect flier"}],"environments":["any (Plane of Gravity)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature resembles a miniature black hole hovering several ft. off the ground. It is a circular region of absolute blackness, with a bizarre distortion around its edges as it warps light waves. Four spiraling, rotating arms of debris and light surround the circular region of darkness. Its facial features are small points of light, almost like stars.","group":"Elemental","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Distortion","kind":"Su","details":"The manipulation of light waves around a gravity elemental grants it a +2 deflection bonus to its Armor Class."},{"type":"Engulf","kind":"Ex","details":"A gravity elemental that starts its turn grappling a creature or holding and object up to one size smaller than itself can absorb the creature or object into its swirling form as a full-round action. An engulfed creature or object takes damage equal to the elemental's slam attack each round it remains engulfed and can take no action other than trying to break free by rolling its CMB vs. the gravity elementals CMD. The gravity elemental gains the grappled condition as long as it has a creature engulfed, and it can only engulf one creature at a time. A creature that dies while engulfed by a gravity elemental is smashed into atoms and can only be restored to life by a miracle, wish, or the intervention of a deity. An object that is destroyed while it is engulfed by a gravity elemental is destroyed forever and cannot be restored. There is a 1% non-cumulative chance each round that an engulfed creature or object is sent to a random plane."},{"type":"Gravity Field","kind":"Su","details":"A gravity elemental's manipulation of gravity function like the reverse gravity and telekinesis spells (CL equal to HD). The maximum weight an Elder gravity elemental can lift with its telekinesis isn't restricted to 375 lbs. The effects of the gravity field are centered on the gravity elemental and move with it. Additionally, by increasing the pull of gravity around itself a gravity elemental can make creatures within a certain radius too heavy to move, or crush them to a pulp. Hold: As a full-round action a gravity elemental can cause all corporeal creatures in its area of effect to become too heavy to move. Creatures in the gravity elemental's gravity field must succeed on a Fortitude save or gain the held condition until the gravity elemental releases them or they break free. A flying creature has a -4 penalty applied to the save; failure means it is unable to remain airborne and must land. The check DC is Strength-based. The gravity elemental can maintain this ability each round as a fullround action. The area of effect and save DC depend on the size of the elemental. If the gravity elemental maintains this ability, on successive rounds a held creature can break free by succeeding on a Strength check with a DC equal to the initial Fortitude save. Any land-bound creature two size categories smaller less than the elemental has its speed automatically reduced by half, even if the Strength check is successful. This ability only works on creatures with weight and mass; incorporeal and gaseous creatures are immune to this power. Crush: Once per day per 2HD, as a standard action, a gravity elemental can increase the gravity around itself to crushing proportions. Anything within the gravity elemental's gravity field takes bludgeoning damage. A successful Fortitude save reduces the damage by half. The area of effect and save DC depend on the elemental's size. The save DC is Strength-based."},{"type":"Immunity to Missile Weapons","kind":"Ex","details":"A gravity elemental is immune to any attack from thrown or hurled weapons, arrows, bolts, stones, and similar weapons with a size equal to or less than its own. Any such ranged attack against a gravity elemental automatically fails and the weapon is pulled into the elemental's body. Captured missiles orbit the gravity elemental's form as long as it desires, and it can release one such missile each round as an improvised thrown weapon. The weapon deals its normal damage plus the gravity elemental's Strength modifier, and has a range increment of 20 ft. A gravity elemental has the Throw Anything feat as a bonus feat."},{"type":"Immunity to Spells","kind":"Ex","details":"A gravity elemental is immune to all spells, spell-like abilities, and effects that depend on weight or mass."},{"type":"Perfect Flier","kind":"Ex","details":"A gravity elemental has perfect control over the forces of gravity, and never needs to make a Fly check when attempting a complex maneuver. It must still make Fly checks to resist external influences on its flight, such as strong winds."}],"description":"A gravity elemental embodies the very force that controls and holds together the fabric of the universe. The actual elemental is a tiny, superdense ball of matter deep within a zone of darkness and spiraling arms of debris that comprise the body of the elemental. A gravity elemental has mass and size, but no effective weight. Gravity elementals originate on a weird, recently discovered plane that scholars affectionately call the Plane of Gravity. The elemental's home plane is a flat, rocky place with little life, no known water sources, and no plant life or foliage. The plane is always shrouded in darkness. Dense pockets of intense gravity and areas of little or no gravity dot the barren landscape. Gravity elementals seem to be able to converse with others of their kind by manipulating gravity itself. Gravity elementals attack primarily by flailing at their opponents with multiple arms, each one a mixture of fluctuating fields of micro-gravity and debris that has been sucked into its gravity well. These creatures can also attack by adjusting the local gravity fields around themselves.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Large Smoke Elemental","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["air","elemental","extraplanar","fire"],"init":10,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":15,"ac_flat_footed":13,"ac_mods":"+6 Dex, +4 natural, -1 size","hp":60,"hd":"8d10+16","hdvalue":8,"fort":8,"ref":12,"will":2,"defensive_abilities":["air mastery","amorphous"],"dr":"5/-","immunities":["elemental traits","fire"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold","vulnerability to wind"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":80,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"2 slams +13 (1d8+3 plus burn)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"burn","details":"1d6, DC 15"},{"type":"engulf","details":"DC 17"}],"strength":16,"dexterity":23,"constitution":15,"intelligence":6,"wisdom":11,"charisma":11,"baseatk":8,"cmb":12,"cmd":28,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":17},{"skill":"Fly","value":23},{"skill":"Perception","value":11},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13,"special":"+21 in smoke or fog"}],"languages":["Auran"],"sq":[{"type":"gaseous"}],"environments":["any (Plane of Air)","any (Plane of Fire)","any (Plane of Smoke)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","gang (3-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"A black cloud of acrid smoke drifts ahead.","group":"Elemental","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Air Mastery","kind":"Ex","details":"Airborne creatures take a -1 penalty on attack and damage rolls against a smoke elemental."},{"type":"Burn","kind":"Ex","details":"A smoke elemental's burn DC includes a -2 racial penalty, as their fires don't burn as hot as a true fire elemental's flames."},{"type":"Engulf","kind":"Ex","details":"A smoke elemental can engulf creatures of its size or smaller into its smoky form as part of a standard action. It cannot make any other attack in which it engulfs. The smoke elemental merely has to move over its opponents, affecting as many as it can cover. Targeted creatures can make attacks of opportunity against the creature, but if they do so, they are not entitled to a saving throw against the engulf attack. Those who don't attempt attacks of opportunity can attempt a Reflex save to avoid being engulfed-on a success, they move back or aside (target's choice). The smoke obscures all sight, including darkvision, beyond 5 ft. and grants concealment to creatures inside the cloud from attacks by opponents that are not adjacent to them. Engulfed opponents don't gain the pinned condition and may move normally. Each round a creature begins its turn engulfed, it suffers from burning eyes (-2 on attack rolls and Perception checks) and takes 3d6 points of fire damage from smoke inhalation. The penalties and damage continue for a number of rounds equal to the smoke elemental's Hit Dice even after escaping the engulf. A creature can make a Fortitude save (DC is listed with each elemental) to end the penalties and damage. The save DCs are Constitution-based."},{"type":"Gaseous","kind":"Ex","details":"A smoke elemental can pass through small holes or narrow openings without reducing its speed."},{"type":"Vulnerability to Wind","kind":"Ex","details":"A smoke elemental is treated as two sizes smaller for purposes of determining the effects high wind has upon it."}],"description":"Smoke elementals are creatures of elemental smoke: part fire, part air. Where the Elemental Plane of Air meets the Elemental Plane of Fire lies a para-elemental plane, that of Elemental Smoke. It is from that black clouded region that these creatures hail.\n\nSmoke elementals spend most of their time on their home plane, only occasionally venturing into the Elemental Planes of Air or Fire. Rarely do they ever enter the Material Plane unless called by a spellcaster.\n\nA smoke elemental appears as a cloud of black smoke or thick fog. No discernible features can be seen in its form, though it can reshape itself at will to form two large eyes and a mouth of empty darkness (which serve no purpose other than to perhaps startle onlookers).","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Large Stingray","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"animal","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":0,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"100 ft."}],"ac":14,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+5 natural, -1 size","hp":68,"hd":"8d8+32","hdvalue":8,"fort":9,"ref":6,"will":3,"speed":[{"type":"swim","speed":30}],"melee":"sting +11 (1d8+6 plus poison), wing +9 (1d6+3)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"poison"}],"strength":22,"dexterity":11,"constitution":17,"intelligence":1,"wisdom":12,"charisma":2,"baseatk":6,"cmb":13,"cmd":23,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (poison)"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":11},{"skill":"Stealth","value":3},{"skill":"Swim","value":14}],"environments":["warm aquatic"],"organizations":["solitary","school (2-5)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"A wide, sail-like creature glides through the water dragging a barbed, whip-like tail behind it.","group":"Stingray","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Sting-injury; save Fort DC 19; frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d2 Str and paralysis 1d6+2 rds.; cure 1 save."}],"description":"Stingrays are bottom feeders and are found in warm, shallow waters near coastlines and shores. They sustain themselves on a diet of plankton, aquatic plants, small crabs, and small fish. Larger stingrays, like smaller rays, are found in shallow, warm waters, though these creatures often swim into much deeper waters. Giant stingrays feed on creatures such as fish, giant crabs, octopus, and sharks. They are more aggressive than their smaller counterparts and often engage prey larger than themselves, relying on their poison to bring down a foe.\n\nFemale stingrays are usually larger than males. Young stingrays resemble adult rays, but are much smaller in size. During birth, the young's pectoral fins are folded against its body but open as soon as it is born.\n\nStingrays are completely flat with no discernible head. At one end is a long, whip-like tail that ends in a razor-sharp and serrated barb. Their eyes appear as small bumps on the end opposite the tail and their mouth is located on the underside of their body. The sides of a stingray are composed of large, wide pectoral fins (mistakenly referred to as wings sometimes). Stingrays are brown, black, or slate gray and their underbelly is white. Small stingrays are about three ft. across, while the largest ray measures 12 ft. across.\n\nSmall stingrays are generally inoffensive creatures. Most \"attacks\" occur in shallow waters when a creature steps on a buried ray. If stepped on, the stingray lashes out with its stinger. If threatened by an opponent much larger than it, the stingray attempts to sting its opponent and then flees.\n\nLarger stingrays are more aggressive than their smaller counterparts, and some are very active when searching for prey. They are nocturnal hunters and attack using a tail sting or wing buffet.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Magnesium Spirit","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["evil","extraplanar","incorporeal","lawful"],"init":6,"ac":14,"ac_touch":14,"ac_flat_footed":12,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +2 deflection, +0 natural","hp":45,"hd":"6d10+18","hdvalue":6,"fort":8,"ref":5,"will":7,"immunities":["incorporeal"],"sr":18,"weaknesses":["vulnerability to holy water"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"incorporeal tail slap +8 (1d6 plus 1d6 Str damage)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"blinding flash"},{"type":"energy drain"},{"type":"soul portal"}],"dexterity":15,"constitution":17,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":15,"charisma":15,"baseatk":6,"cmb":8,"cmd":20,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (soul portal)"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":11},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":8},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":10},{"skill":"Perception","value":11},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":11},{"skill":"Stealth","value":11},{"skill":"Survival","value":8}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature looks like a human-sized column of white fire with a wispy tail protruding from the bottom of it.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Energy Drain","kind":"Su","details":"A magnesium spirit possessing a host deals 1 negative level to it each round if the host fails a DC 16 Will save. A magnesium spirit gains 5 temporary hit points for each negative level bestowed. The save DC is Constitutionbased. Negative levels remain for 24 hours, after which time the host can attempt a DC 16 Fortitude save to remove a negative level."},{"type":"Soul Portal","kind":"Su","details":"This ability is similar to a magic jar spell (caster level 8th), except that it doesn't require a receptacle. To use this ability, the magnesium spirit must try move into the target's space; moving into the target's space to use this ability doesn't provoke attacks of opportunity. The target can resist the attack with a successful DC 17 Will save. If the save fails, the magnesium spirit vanishes into the target's body. The save DC is Charisma-based and includes a +2 bonus from the creature's Ability Focus feat. A magnesium spirit that has possessed an opponent's body deals a negative level to the host each round (see its energy drain attack above). When the host drops below 1st level, both it and the magnesium spirit vanish in a flash of white light as the spirit completes the ritual needed to return it to its plane of origin. Neither is ever seen again. Each round, as a standard action, while the magnesium spirit inhabits its body, the host can attempt to eject the creature by making an opposed Wisdom check against the magnesium spirit's Wisdom check. If successful, the magnesium spirit is ejected and cannot use its soul portal ability against that creature again for 1 hour. A magnesium spirit can be damaged by holy water even while merged with its host. Holy water deals 2d4 points of damage per vial to the creature. If it takes half or more of its current hit points in damage from holy water, it is ejected from the host's body. The host is stunned for 1d3 rounds."},{"type":"Strength Damage","kind":"Su","details":"A magnesium spirit's incorporeal tail slap deals 1d6 points of Strength damage to a living foe. When a foe has taken a total of Strength damage equal to one-half its original Strength total, the magnesium spirit can use its soul portal attack against that opponent."},{"type":"Vulnerability to Holy Water","kind":"Ex","details":"A magnesium spirit takes 2d4 points of damage from holy water (even while merged with a host)."}],"description":"The magnesium spirit is an evil creature from an unknown plane, though it is agreed among sages that its origin definitely doesn't lie on the Material Plane. Believed to have been summoned by wizards or sorcerers to do their bidding, the magnesium spirit desires nothing more than to return to its home plane. Its incorporeal form prevents this, however, and it requires a physical body to complete the spell ritual needed to return it home. A magnesium spirit attacks first by attempting to blind its opponents before attacking with its incorporeal tail slap. Once it has dealt the requisite Strength damage to a foe, it uses its soul portal ability against that target. A magnesium spirit's natural weapons, as well as any weapons it wields, are treated as evil-aligned and lawful-aligned for the purposes of overcoming damage reduction.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Magnesium Spirit originally appeared in the First Edition Fiend Folio (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1981) and is used by permission."}];
